# WFORMTT.KEY - the pick lists of the form dialog (WPICK) and the item
# form's location field; TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WFORMTT.SNP.
# F3 opens item 1 (at Office, OFF) in edit mode; Alt+L reaches its
# Location, whose path shows under it.  F4 opens the location tree on
# Office; TAB and SHIFT-TAB cycle list, OK and Cancel; Shelf A1 chosen
# puts A1 in the field and its path under it, the focus staying there.
# ALT+DOWN, as F4, opens it again on Shelf A1; the first row, (no
# location), empties the field; Esc in the list leaves the field as it
# was.
K F3 ALT-L
S FIELD
K F4
S LOC
K TAB
S TAB1
K TAB
S TAB2
K TAB
S TAB3
K STAB
S STAB1
K STAB
S STAB2
K STAB
S STAB3
K DOWN ENTER
S CHOSEN
K ALT-DOWN
S ONVALUE
K HOME ENTER
S NOLOC
K F4 ESC
S CANCEL
# A code that names no location, typed and left: "No location ZZ"
# under the fields and no path; OK then stops on the field.  0 empties
# it, the path (no location), the message gone.
T ZZ
K TAB
S NOSUCH
K ENTER
S OKSTOP
T 0
K TAB
S ZERO
# the form is changed, so Esc asks: Yes leaves it
K ESC
S ASK
K Y
# view mode: CTRL+E switches to edit mode and opens no list
K F4 CTRL-E
S VIEWF4
K ESC
# the item form opens on Category, whose F4 opens the category list on
# the item's category; Esc closes it, and Esc the unchanged form
K F3 F4
S CAT
K ESC ESC
# the category list's fetch refused by the disk, the session kept:
# Category is a code field with a pick list, whose F4 opens the category
# list on the item's category; Esc closes it, and Esc the unchanged form
K CTRL-F3
S CATFAIL
K F4
S CATPICK
K ESC ESC
# the session ended under the item form: the category list's fetch finds
# it out, its box over the frame
K F9 F4
S ENDPICK
K ESC
S ENDED
